According to a psychological study, they claim that Free Fire is Bad for minors. How true is this?
The first ones were created in the 50s and since then they have evolved to become an everyday tool. This phenomenon has evidenced that there are different factors that can modify behavior, due to the learning that the player has acquired in the different audiovisual stimuli.
The findings indicate that spending an hour or two playing games provides academic and cognitive benefits.
If the time of manipulation of video games is not controlled, it will be an addiction disorder according to the World Health Organization. WHO encoded video game use disorder as 6C51 in the International Classification of Diseases (ICD 11).
This game encourages social interaction, both real and virtual. You form plans and strategy in real time, having to cooperate with your companions to help each other achieve victory.
The corresponding aptitudes, abilities and skills on the part of each team member will depend on this to promote communication, commitment and coordination. These characteristics that have not only serve to play, but also for important factors such as working life.
It also provides you with the ability to increase your skills, in addition to learning to overcome the frustration of losing in a game. It teaches that to be a champion you have to practice every day and give your best, as in any competition.
According to psychology, there are three phases of video game addiction that modify behavior:
At this stage there is still no deep emotional involvement; and the user is simply adjusting to the commitment to the virtual world.
Here the player's emotion is affected. The narrative or the effects draw the player's attention by profoundly altering their emotions.
This expression refers to who uses the game to protect themselves from or escape from the real world.
After these three stages, addiction is created in the player, dedicating large amounts of hours to the game and affecting his behavior. Addiction usually causes aggressive episodes, visual stimulation of the video game usually causes an impulsive response that leads to loss of track of time.
A consensus can be reached that any negative aspect that may arise is part of the family problem, an adolescent who lacks the attention of the parents is more likely to immerse himself in an unhealthy gambling habit.
