You should never pronounce the name as 'fre fire' this is a fairly common mistake among first-time users who have just finished downloading the game, they haven't had much connection with it and obviously aren't given much English either.
And the third way to pronounce the name of the game is something peculiar and a little less popular because they call it 'fri fai' and it is a bit strange, since this form is almost correct, but for some reason users forget the last letter R.
Among other incorrect ways of calling it are, 'fri fa', 'fri faia' 'fri fir'.
Basically these are the fails in the pronunciation of the free fire game from its users around the world.
This is the complement of the main name of the game, it is a much more complex word and therefore its pronunciation much more difficult, the correct way to do it would be something like 'Barolgraunds' placing accent and pronunciation in English.
Because the game was born in an Asian country, many wonder why it doesn't have a name in Mandarin Chinese or a similar language?
To which the creators of the game saw an opportunity to place a much more global name, since their mission was undoubtedly to be recognized beyond its eastern borders.
So if the game were in Spanish its name would be 'Free Fire in Battlefields' quite striking in both English and Spanish.
On the other hand, the word 'free' wants to let users know that they have an open field and they will be able to be free to open fire on the opponent they want and they will be able to move around the board as they wish.
Finally 'battlefields' although it is a little known complement, it offers players both the knowledge of the theme of the game and the place where its development will take place.
This term refers to a certain group of Free Fire players who have a high level of play, who eliminate their rivals quickly and accurately.
Many people prefer this add-on over Battlegrounds, perhaps because of the pronunciation, its extension or because it was originally called in beta 1 and they consider it to be its original name.
Shooter is a game classification mode, its meaning is 'shooter', its pronunciation is 'Shurer'
Winterlands is the game's winter event, its translation 'winter lands' its pronunciation 'winterlans'.
Updates means 'updates' its pronunciation is 'apdes'
Aidrop as objects always fall until your avatar is 'delivery by parachute' pronunciation 'eirdrap'
If you were one of the people who mispronounced the name of your favorite game or some of its accessories, don't worry, you just learned everything about their names and the correct way to call them.
