For some years with the expansion of mobile devices and Apps, countless games have emerged in the play store, among these the most downloaded are the Battle Royale games, among which popularity is currently disputed by two of them, Fortnite and Free Fire in this article we will briefly talk about them, history, similarities and differences. Who will win the battle?
This video game was developed by the American company Epic Game based in North Carolina, its launch took place on June 25, 2017, at first it was launched as a game with different software packages which allowed different game modes although they all share the same search engine and the same game mechanics.
The other version is Fortnite save the world This version is a cooperative game where the objective is to eliminate the (husks) which are nothing but zombies created by the strange violet storm that surrounds the earth. Players fight these husks by protecting themselves from the storm with storm shields as they search for weapons and items with which to kill the zombies.
Since these two games are on the market, they dispute the first place of preference and as the shooter with the most downloads on Android, but despite their popularity, each one differs from the other in several aspects that we will mention below:
Gameplay: Although the gameplay of both games is similar, they have some differences, in Fornite you can start the game by building a protection hut against enemies, while in Free Fire you must start collecting weapons once you land on the battlefield and you must cover yourself with what you can. The gameplay is similar, what varies are the game strategies and missions.
Battlefield: while in Free Fire you have a battlefield where you can wait and launch stealth missions and surprise attacks in Fortnite you are subject to constant and unforeseen weather changes due to the storm.
Both games are third person shooter
