Well here the fundamental thing is not to abandon your life for nothing, and less for a game, you should always take it as a hobby that you do in your free time without leaving your responsibilities and personal relationships aside.
While it is true that the game can improve your attention levels, give you more agility in your reflexes, and why not get rid of boredom for a while, like all things in excess, playing Free Fire for a long time can become the nightmare of your life.
That all this will happen without you realizing it, we could say that it is something like a vice.
All these circumstances so far are rumors of players, but there is no confirmation about it.
There are several difficulties that the game has, most of all related to the psychological part of its users.
Several parents who have been consulted on this topic have had similar responses, and it is that children are presenting isolation, aggressiveness, anxiety, among other abnormal behaviors, all this from knowing and starting the Free Fire game in their mobile devices.
Parents have chosen to prohibit gambling or remove minors from their cell phones, but they have reacted aggressively, crying and hitting objects.
They do not have fun on breaks because they remain introverted with their cell phones in hand.
Professionals assure that the only ones responsible are the parents of the minors, because they should be aware of what their children do on cell phones and have strict control over it.
This is because many times they grow up with the mentality of wanting to make the game come true and from this condition different massacres have been derived in history.
Experts who have thoroughly investigated the game say that this condition is due to the fact that the slogan of the game is that 'your adrenaline will rise the more opponents you kill', which sometimes people tend to bring to reality.
The habit of not being able to leave the game for a minute has led some youth and adult countries to be run over for going out on the street looking at their cell phones, as they cross the avenues without any precaution, pending their departure as well as using headphones.
Many children have taken refuge in this game so much that the fact of losing games considers it as a great disappointment, which they have not been able to overcome, and because of bullying and the personal grief of defeat they unfortunately choose to take their own lives.
And it is a reality that almost all children today have cell phones and the vast majority of parents do not have clear control over the applications they use on them.
Not really, since there are also difficulties that adults can have, many of them related to excessive spending of money on gambling, which sometimes leads to difficulties with the family in terms of economy.
It is equally important to take into account the handling of the information authorized on these platforms and remind users that personal or financial information should not be given to any other user of the game.
