The G18 is one of the most common weapons in Free Fire, being a good option until we find a better weapon. The Desert Eagle can be used for long-range fire and can be given a muzzle and silencer.
The USP is really light and can be handled well without affecting player agility. Lastly, the M500 is recommended for running long distance players due to its 2x range and high range.
For fast strategy and short-range combat, the MP40 is one of the most widely used due to its high rate of fire and damage. The P90 is also good for rushing due to its high shooting speed and magazine storage.
The M1014 and SPAS12 are shotguns with high damage rates, but the SPAS12 has a higher firing rate and reload speed, and may have a larger clip size. To use the SPAS12 with confidence, a player must practice using it in different situations, because it is a one shot weapon.
The UMP has low precision, but has a high rate of fire, so it might be good for early play.
For medium and long range games, rifles are one of the best options. The GROZA could be considered one of the best weapons in the game, as it is stable, has great damage and can be found by any player.
The M4A1 is considered easy to use and suitable for beginners due to its low recoil rate. AK and FAMAS are one of the best-known weapons in shooting games.
The crossbow is similar to the M249 in that it is only found in aerial launches. It does not receive attackers, but it is a good option for closed places with a high concentration of enemies, since its damage can affect more than one player at a time but must be protected during the recharge time.
The SKS is pre-attached with a 4x scope, which could be an advantage. Additionally, DRAGUNOV is almost as powerful as AWM, but is only available at refueling points and air launches.
There is a fundamental difference to the system used to define a cartridge caliber between a weapon with the anima (the interior of the barrel) smooth, and the employee for the weapons with the lined soul.
These are used by weapons whose bore is scratched, such as AK47, SKS, M14. AR bullets have a higher caliber, so they will do more damage and have better precision in long distance shots.
These are the bullets used by weapons like the MP40, MP5, and VSS. They are of a low caliber, so they do more damage over short distances.
