These rifles are easily the deadliest type of weapon in Free Fire, if we know how to use them and we have a good pulse, we can lower many points of life to our enemy, or even cause a immediate death.
The ideal is to use them as a secondary weapon, having as primary a assault rifle since it is ideal for both medium and short distances. Although if you are very confident in your skills, you can carry a shotgun to quickly get out of confrontations with enemies that are very close.
The main attraction of these weapons lies in their Damage / Range / Aim ratio not only do they have an incomparable range, but they hit the target we are aiming for in the distance without the need to equip them with any accessory to improve them.
The damage capacity these weapons have is barely exceeded by that of the shotguns, and for very few points. They are arguably two sides of the same coin, as one easily kills a nearby enemy, the other does so from a safe distance.
Sniper rifles are incredibly powerful weapons, but they are not a piece of cake to use. You have to be very careful when shooting not to miss the shot, as it could be the end of the game for us.
Although this weapon is considered a combination of an assault rifle and a submachine gun, its appearance, as well as its range and precision, are worthy of a sniper rifle.
The SKS is the automatic rifle, but it is the least accurate of all due to its high recoil. Luckily it can carry a front grip and recoil reduction tip, as well as a larger capacity magazine.
The Kar98K comes pre-equipped with an x8 sight which makes it extremely efficient. If we find it during the first minutes of the game and we don't have many enemies nearby, it will give us a lot of advantage.
The only bad thing about it is that it is only available in drops, because not even its firing and loading speed represent a disadvantage; a shot we hit is practically a kill safe.
There is no doubt that sniper rifles are a weapon that we must take into account in our games. Have you ever used one?
