The history of industrial aluminum profile -- from aluminum profile manufacturer fscyal.com
Industrial aluminum profile is an indispensable basic raw material in the national economy and is widely used in construction, packaging, transportation, power and other fields.
In 1746, German scientist Porter made anodized industrial aluminum profiles from alum.
The Englishman David taught the melting and oxidizing of industrial aluminum profiles to obtain metal.
In 1809 David named the envisioned metal Alumium and later changed it to Aluminium.
The invention of the Bayer method for the production of oxidized industrial aluminum profiles from industrial aluminum profiles, clay and ore, and the progress of DC electrolytic technology have laid the foundation for the development of industrial aluminum profiles to industrial scale.
The price of industrial aluminum profiles has fallen thousands of times.
This pioneering move enables industrial aluminum profiles to be produced on a large scale and lays down the industrial method of aluminum profiles in the world's electrolytic industry today.
Automotive engines have begun to use industrial aluminum alloy castings, and the shipbuilding industry has also begun to use industrial aluminum alloy alloy plates, profiles, and castings.
Extensive, greatly stimulated the development of industrial aluminum profile industry.
German A. Wilm invented the hard industrial aluminum profile alloy (Al-Cu-Mg alloy) in 1906, which doubled the strength of industrial aluminum profiles.
These alloys have different characteristics and functions The use of industrial aluminum profiles has been greatly expanded, and the application of industrial aluminum profiles in industrial sectors such as construction, automobiles, railways, ships and aircraft manufacturing has been rapidly developed.
The world's industrial aluminum profile output has increased to more than 45,000 tons.
In 1943, the total output of the original industrial aluminum profile soared to 2 million tons.
However, as the major industrial aluminum profile companies actively developed new civilian products, the application of industrial aluminum profiles was gradually promoted to instruments , Electronics, transportation, daily hardware, food packaging and other fields, increasing the demand for industrial aluminum profiles year by year.
The world's industrial aluminum production exceeds copper, ranking first in non-ferrous metals.
The world's primary industrial aluminum profile production has exceeded 16 million tons, and the recycled industrial aluminum profile consumption has reached 4.5 million tons.
The processing of industrial aluminum profiles mainly includes forming and surface processing.
Forming process There are roughly two methods for processing and forming aluminum alloys: extrusion and rolling.
Inrtroduce of aluminium profile company history in China (2)
In this article, you can see the how the aluminium profile company develop in China.
In the 1980s, more than 20 years since the 1980s (1980s and 1990s), China's townships and privately-run aluminum profiles factories have been the flourishing period for the rapid development of aluminum profiles in China.
At present, these enterprises, including township and village enterprises, have basically turned into private private enterprises and become the main force of China's construction aluminum profile industry today.
Due to the differences in the economic environment at the time, the development in the South was fast and the scale became early.
Dalian Liaoning Aluminum Factory in northern Liaoning Province, Sun Yongzhen, the director of the factory; Wuxian Aluminum Processing Factory in East China Suzhou (now converted to Taiwan-funded Suzhou Luopusjin Aluminum Co., Ltd. ), Factory director Wu Alu; Xingfa Aluminum Factory in Nanhai, Guangdong (now one of the seven famous enterprises in the field of aluminum profiles in China), factory director Luo Su, the three star township enterprises and Star township entrepreneurs.
In the 1990s, the mainland economy rose, and construction aluminum companies gradually began to develop in coastal provinces.
As a result, the Pearl River Delta in the southern part of Guangdong and the South China Sea, the Yangtze River Delta in the eastern part of Jiangsu and Zhejiang, and the Bohai Bay in the northern part of Liaoning and Shandong are the three areas where aluminum profiles are developed.
Today, Dali is centered on aluminum profiles, which constitutes the industry chain of production support, equipment, spare parts, raw materials, and auxiliary materials in China's aluminum profile industry and related industries.
Then Foshan has become the most dense area of aluminum profile factories, and its industrial chain is more complete.
, The construction aluminum profile industry adapted to market demand, and was able to develop and improve rapidly.
By the end of February 2005, they had officially received national construction The number of aluminum profile production license companies is 459 (building type companies need to apply for production licenses from the state), and private enterprises are the absolute main body.
They are the most developed, and the industrial chain is well developed.
By the end of 2005, the number of companies that had obtained building aluminum production permits increased to 485, but in recent years, some companies in Guangdong and the mainland have also stopped production.
New aluminum extrusion plants in the Yangtze River Delta (Jiangsu-Zhejiang) and Bohai Bay (Luji-Liao) areas have been growing intensively.
In 2005, according to the regulations of the General Administration of Quality Supervision, Inspection and Quarantine and the National Standardization Administration Committee, from March 1st, the new standard "Aluminum Alloy Building Profile" GB5237-2004 was officially implemented, replacing the original aluminum alloy building profile standard GB5237-2000.
The content includes six parts: substrate, anodizing, colored profiles, electrophoretic painted profiles, powder sprayed profiles, fluorocarbon paint sprayed profiles, and thermal insulation profiles, and requires manufacturers to enforce them.
Products that do not meet mandatory standards will be banned from production, sale and import.
This is more conducive to the management of aluminum profiles and its application in the construction market.
The thickness level of the anodized film should be selected according to the use environment, and its requirements should meet the standard requirements and be specified in the contract.
The coating adhesion shall reach 0 level after the cross-cut test, and the dry, wet and boiling water adhesion of the coating shall reach 0 level.
Seven, concluding remarks
The development and promotion of window types and structures will have more requirements for aluminum production.
Aluminum for construction is always the first choice in foreign countries.
Their construction industry has become saturated.
China ’s construction industry is still developing.
will bring a large number of venues and facilities and related For construction projects, aluminum doors and windows, curtain walls, and structural aluminum are still favored by the construction market, and the prospect of building materials continues to be promising.
