However, due to the problem of 3D film source, the sales volume of 3D TV in the market is not ideal, and the content has become the biggest bottleneck of 3D TV popularization.
According to the method of observing things by human eyes, 3D films are shot by two cameras simultaneously.
When people watch the 3D images, the double images are reconnected with corresponding 3D glasses, so as to show a coherent three-dimensional picture and let the audience have the magical illusion of immersing themselves.
Although 3D film technology has been mature, there are still many people who want to save time or are not willing to invest more money to shoot with 2D method, and then use computer software to divide the images into different levels and stagger them slightly, so as to realize the three-dimensional effect.
Although the biggest problem facing the 3D industry is the lack of content, it does not mean to connive at the “Pseudo 3D” content.
In the long run, the producers’ eagerness for quick success and instant profits is not conducive to the development of 3D films, and will do harm to the development of 3D industry in the future.
At present, some brands have launched new flat panel TV products with the function of 2D to 3D, which can convert ordinary 2D film source into 3D film source.
The 2D to 3D function of flat panel TV is calculated and converted by internal software, which is the same as Pseudo 3D source, and even worse in effect.
For example, the battle of the gods, if measured by the standard of an ordinary 2D film, its production level is still good, but the audience has to watch “Pseudo 3D”.
