in the selection and use of LED display screen, we should pay attention to the following aspects:
At present, the point spacing of LED display screen used in domestic TV studio is mostly 6-8 mm.
Fill factor of LED display is also called bright area ratio, that is, the ratio of luminous area of each pixel to the physical surface area of the pixel.
If the light source is limited in a very small pixel surface area, the brightness of a single pixel is several times or even more than ten times of the whole screen brightness, it will cause a more serious glare.
At present, many LED displays in the market have not reached this index.
With the increase of fill factor, the viewing angle of the display screen is wider and the color mixing effect is more ideal.
Jiangsu Education station selects the LED display screen with filling factor of 60%.
According to the program requirements, the lighting in the studio sometimes uses 3200K low color temperature lamps, sometimes uses 5600k high color temperature lamps, and the LED display screen needs to be adjusted to the corresponding color temperature, so as to obtain satisfactory shooting effect.
The distance between the person being photographed and the screen is 4-10 meters, so that we can get a better background picture.
As an integrated electronic product, LED display screen is mainly composed of control board with electronic components, switching power supply, light-emitting devices, etc., and the life and stability of all these components are closely related to the working temperature.
A large amount of dust will be produced in the transformation of the studio, so it is necessary to protect the LED display screen in advance.
