Therefore, how to improve the reliability and stability of signal transmission has become a subject that engineers have to face.
Therefore, the choice of transmission medium is particularly important.
We can regard RS-485 transmission cable as an equivalent circuit composed of several resistors, inductors and capacitors.
In addition to signal attenuation, another factor affecting signal transmission is signal reflection.
The reason for the reflection is that when the communication line is idle, the signal of the whole communication line is disorderly.
Our usual solution is to add the A and B wires of RS-485 bus with a certain resistance value of bias resistance, and pull them up and down respectively, so that there will be no unpredictable random signals.
When the signal suddenly meets the cable at the end of the transmission line, the impedance is very small or even not, and the signal will reflect at this place.
Since the signal transmission on the cable is bidirectional, a terminal resistor of the same size should also be bridged at the other end of the communication cable.
Because the signal transmitted on RS-485 bus is composed of innumerable “1” and “0” bits, when encountering special bytes such as 0x01, the level “0” makes the distributed capacitor get sufficient time to charge.
A simple and reliable RS-485 communication protocol is developed for LED display screen.
In the early stage of the project, whether the generic cabling is professional (for example, the signal line should keep a certain distance from the power line), the indeterminacy of the communication distance, the degree of interference around the communication line, whether the communication line adopts twisted shielded wire, etc., all these factors have a great impact on the normal communication of the system.
