A – Si: H thin films exposed to strong light or electric current for a long time will produce defects in the films, which leads to the degradation of the performance of the films, which is called the steabler wronski effect.
At present, amorphous silicon materials have become a hot topic at home and abroad.
The defect mode will affect the position of Fermi energy level of – Si: H thin film material, which will change the distribution of electrons and cause the change of optical properties.
These defects become additional recombination centers of electrons and holes, resulting in the increase of electron capture cross section and the shortening of electron lifetime
The bond energy of these bonds is very large and is not easy to break.
The chemical potential of high strain Si Si bond is equivalent to that of H, which can be broken by external energy to form Si-H bond or to form stronger Si Si bond.
In order to better understand the mechanism and control of the influence of S-W and find a stable treatment method and technology, scientists at home and abroad have made unremitting efforts for more than 20 years, and put forward a large number of physical models, mainly including weak bond fracture (SJT) model, “H” glass model, collision model, si-h-h model, if the bridge bond form “defectpool” mode, But there is still no unified view.
